      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i'm looking at some ceramic fragments from a late helladic layer and i'm having trouble distinguishing between different firing techniques based on the surface. can u explain what i should be looking for to tell if a piece was fired in an oxidizing vs reducing atmosphere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "When distinguishing between oxidizing and reducing firings in Late Helladic ceramic fragments, observe the surface coloration. Oxidizing firings typically produce a more glassy, shiny surface with a green or yellow-green patina (glaze-like appearance), as iron oxides are heated to form iron(III) oxide. Reducing firings, on the other hand, usually exhibit a matte, earthy surface color with a brown or pinkish hue due to the presence of iron oxides being reduced to iron metal.",
